.TH EXPORTCODE 1 "November 2026" "ExportCode 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ExportCode \- export source code into AI\-friendly text chunks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B exportcode
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIROOT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ExportCode
walks
.I ROOT
(default: the current directory) recursively, so every subfolder is included,
reads all text files it finds and writes them to one or more text files.
Each file is introduced by a marker line, a project tree is placed at the top,
and the output is split into chunks of a configurable size so that it can be
pasted into an AI chat window piece by piece.
.PP
While running, every file found is listed by its path relative to
.IR ROOT .
Exported files are prefixed with
.B +
and skipped files with
.B \-
followed by the reason in parentheses. Directories that were not entered
are listed once, with a trailing slash.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Arguments
.TP
.I ROOT
Project folder to export. Defaults to the current directory.
.SS Selecting files
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-ext\fR \fIEXT\fR...
Only export files with these extensions. The leading dot is optional
(\fBpy\fR and \fB.py\fR are equal). Without this option all text files are
exported.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR \fIFILE\fR...
Also include files with these exact names, for example
.BR CMakeLists.txt .
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-exclude\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR...
Folder names, relative paths or shell globs to skip.
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-file\fR \fIPATTERN\fR...
File globs to skip, for example \fB*.min.js\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-default\-excludes
Do not skip the folders listed under
.BR "DEFAULT EXCLUDES" .
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-file\-kb\fR \fIKB\fR
Skip files larger than this many kilobytes. Default: 500.
.SS Output
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
Output file. Default:
.BI ./ NAME _export.txt
in the current directory, where
.I NAME
is the name of
.IR ROOT .
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-chunk\-size\fR \fICHARS\fR
Maximum number of characters per chunk. Default: 60000.
.TP
.B \-\-split\-output
Write one file per chunk (\fINAME\fB_1.txt\fR, \fINAME\fB_2.txt\fR, ...)
instead of a single file.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Keep whitespace untouched. By default trailing spaces and runs of blank lines
are removed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tree
Omit the project structure from the first chunk.
.SS Terminal display
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Do not list files; print only the summary.
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-skipped
List only exported files.
.SS Other
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the built\-in help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and exit.
.SH SKIP REASONS
.TP
.B excluded directory
The folder matches a default exclude or \fB\-\-exclude\-dir\fR.
.TP
.B excluded file pattern
The file matches \fB\-\-exclude\-file\fR.
.TP
.B extension not selected
Filtered out by \fB\-\-ext\fR / \fB\-\-name\fR.
.TP
.B larger than N KB
Bigger than \fB\-\-max\-file\-kb\fR.
.TP
.B binary file
Contains NUL bytes (images, archives, executables, ...).
.TP
.B empty file
Nothing but whitespace.
.TP
.B previous export output
Looks like an earlier output file from the same run location.
.TP
.B export tool
The ExportCode script or its \fBsrc\fR folder.
.SH DEFAULT EXCLUDES
These folder names are skipped at any depth unless
.B \-\-no\-default\-excludes
is given:
\&.git, \&.svn, \&.hg, \&.idea, \&.vscode, \&.vs, node_modules, __pycache__,
\&.venv, venv, env, build, dist, out, bin, obj, target, \&.mypy_cache,
\&.pytest_cache, \&.cache, \&.gradle.
.SH EXAMPLES
Export the current project, all subfolders included:
.PP
.RS
.nf
exportcode
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only Python and Markdown files, written to a chosen file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
exportcode ~/proj \-e py md \-o ~/proj.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
C++ project with CMake files, skipping tests and minified files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
exportcode ~/proj \-e cpp h \-n CMakeLists.txt \e
    \-x tests \-\-exclude\-file "*.min.js"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Small chunks, one file each, summary only:
.PP
.RS
.nf
exportcode . \-c 30000 \-\-split\-output \-q
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Options that take several values (\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-n\fR, \fB\-x\fR,
\fB\-\-exclude\-file\fR) consume every following word. Give
.I ROOT
before them, or end the list with
.BR \-\- .
.PP
Colors are used when writing to a terminal; set
.B NO_COLOR
to disable them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one file was exported.
.TP
.B 1
.I ROOT
is not a directory, or no matching files were found.
.SH INSTALLATION
View without installing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
man ./man/ExportCode.1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install for the current user:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.local/share/man/man1
cp man/ExportCode.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/
.fi
.RE
